{"item_id": "feed:https://www.treelinereview.com/gearreviews/brawyn-essential-supreme-bra-review", "version_id": "d31e9f337a8af67a512cb7f07814e94acf86a69cdd3058918f2608d24de42d6d", "decision": "reject", "reason": "Under the Relevance section, sports bras fall outside the listed in-scope categories (clothing and protection covers tactical clothing, rain and cold-weather layers, eye protection, and holsters, not intimate apparel), and the item is a single-author, affiliate-linked review with no Mammoth connection. Under Credibility and Commercial incentives, the claims rest on one tester's personal wear experience and the piece is affiliate-supported, with no independent publisher corroboration.", "piece_ids": []}
{"item_id": "feed:https://www.treelinereview.com/gearreviews/saucony-ride-19-road-running-shoes-review", "version_id": "604f165566c4bf6d642e8f64e8f389f0249566605ac8dcdbd6175011909feb96", "decision": "defer", "reason": "Road running shoes fall within the rucking and endurance gear category, and the review reports over 100 miles of testing with specific durability and weight figures, so it is relevant. However, the review is a single affiliate-linked outlet with no Mammoth-specific conditions (loaded carry, multi-day use), and its central claims about cushioning and durability are the publisher's own observations without independent corroboration, so the evidence is too thin to rely on under the Credibility and Commercial incentives sections.", "piece_ids": []}
{"item_id": "feed:https://www.treelinereview.com/gearreviews/best-walking-shoes", "version_id": "e629098f36e81f676d9c57f5a0980758b87d7fb36153363d10bc430d87696bdc", "decision": "reject", "reason": "The item is a general women's walking-shoe buying guide focused on office shifts, plantar fasciitis, and travel rather than Mammoth conditions, so it fails the Relevance section's emphasis on carried weight, durability under load, and multi-day performance. It is also affiliate-supported and cites its own testers without independent corroboration, and it offers no Mammoth-specific evidence.", "piece_ids": []}
{"item_id": "feed:https://www.treelinereview.com/gearreviews/lems-zenspeed-plus-road-running-shoes-review", "version_id": "15a35cd64abe2d51730f5051a2208c0645f58664091d4c9e6b7775be16b6c63f", "decision": "defer", "reason": "Road running shoes are an in-scope rucking and endurance category, and the review reports 100+ miles across varied surfaces with specific measured figures (weight, stack height, drop), which is relevant. However, the evidence rests on a single affiliate-supported publisher with no independent corroboration and no Mammoth-specific loaded or multi-day testing, so under the Credibility and Commercial incentives sections it is too thin to rely on yet.", "piece_ids": []}
